Not a fold divergence - a float RENDERING one, and the same one bootstrap/
README.md lists among the four where the bootstrap is the correct side.

The reference interpolates a float through `%f` and prints six decimal places:

  ROOT_16=4.000000 TWO_10=1024.000000 HYPOT=5.000000
  FLOOR_D=3.000000 CEIL_D=4.000000 ABS_D=7.000000

The bootstrap prints the value. Every folded NUMBER agrees - the two compilers
compute the same bits, because both of them call the same libm rather than
modelling it - so the parity worth having here is already asserted by
comptime.test.yoop, which checks the emitted constant as a hex bit pattern
(`0x4014000000000000`) rather than as a rendering.

The integer half of the fixture agrees with the reference exactly, including
`strcmp` normalizing to -1 / 0 / 1.
